==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Faster health regeneration and fast speed at night, although speed still slower than the [[Rabbit]] race.
* The player can change their race back to Ghoul whenever they'd like; no need to pay anything.
* Very good with [[Buddha]] due to the race's life leech. ([[Sanguine Art]] is also recommended due to additional life leech.) Also, with the second blue gear crows can lure nearby npcs easily, making grinding easier principally with [[Buddha]].
* It can be considered as a mixture of all [[Races]], having faster [[health]] regeneration ([[Angel]]) and faster speed ([[Rabbit]]) at night, as well as extra defense ([[Shark]]/[[Cyborg]]), extra damage (not by much however) ([[Human]]/[[Cyborg]]), and area control/support. ([[Draco]]) These benefits help in making it a good choice for people who can't decide on which race they want to use.
* Any moves in cooldown below 40% will be renewed when awakening.

|'''[[Heightened Senses]] (V3)'''
* Nearly halves cooldowns (-40%), making moves very spammable and allowing for quick comebacks in PvP.
* Offers decent mobility, especially when paired with the nighttime speed boost.
* Balanced ability, as it buffs damage, speed, and defense.
* Lasts for 8 seconds.

|'''Blood Siphon (V4)'''
* Gives life leech for all damage sources.
* Good for long fights.
** Makes fights against [[bosses]] easier.
* Great for healing quickly.
* Good for PvP scenarios where there is more than one opponent.
* Can reduce the effectiveness of [[Draco#Changes_of_Stages|Draco]]'s Thorn Mail, although the life leech will be lost.
* Provides strong healing in PvE scenarios when consistently dealing damage, making it highly useful in [[Raids]], particularly for [[Buddha]] users.

|'''Domain Expansion (V4)'''
* Reduces cooldowns.
* Grants speed buffs during daytime, rivaling even races like [[Rabbit]] with certain [[accessories]].
* Negates enemies' [[health]] regen by a significant amount, rendering them only capable of healing 1 [[Health]] point at a time, to the point where each gain in health is countable.
* Deals damage to close enemies while dashing. Repeatedly dashing around the enemy can deal significant damage in just a few seconds.
* Crows consume enemy [[Instinct]], and can completely drain it during combos.
** Can deal damage to sky campers up until a certain height limit.
* Can easily lure [[NPCs]] with the crows just by dashing near them
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* [[Life Leech]] only affects [[Fighting Styles]], making it less useful for other builds.
** Heals 5 times less on [[Enemies|enemy NPCs]].
* More tedious to obtain than some other [[races]]. (Hellfire Torch is chance-based, and can only be obtained by defeating a raid boss.)

|'''[[Heightened Senses]] (V3)'''
* Rather weak defense.

|'''Blood Siphon (V4)'''
* Gives life leech for all damage sources but doesn't guarantee full heals and can be minimal sometimes.

|'''Domain Expansion (V4)'''
* Can be countered by keeping distance.
* Requires dashing around the enemy multiple times to deal high damage.
* Dark effects can negatively affect allies.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==

* A Ghoul V3 user having the [[Dino Hood]] equipped can outrun a [[Rabbit]] V3 user having the [[Pilot Helmet]] equipped. But cannot outrun a Rabbit v3 who also has the Dino Hood.
* Ghoul V3 does not allow you to bypass the automatic cooldown placed on (V) moves upon spawning in.
* This is the only race that allows the user to reset all moves when awakening (similar to the race's skill)
* When in V4 with the Ghoul race, the user has visible black skulls floating upward on the player. This relates to ghouls race logo found in the Temple of Time.

